---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
import { drift } from '../data/content';

// What the licence card shows before and after each change.
const rows = [
  { key: 'model', dt: 'Model', was: 'v1.0, tested', now: 'v1.1, updated overnight' },
  { key: 'data', dt: 'Data', was: 'CRM records, 2025', now: '+ three new sources' },
  { key: 'permissions', dt: 'Permissions', was: 'Suggest replies', now: 'Send replies and refunds' },
  { key: 'use', dt: 'Use', was: 'Customer service', now: '+ hiring decisions' },
];
---
<section class="section gap" id="gap" aria-labelledby="gap-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead n="01" label="The gap" id="gap-title">
      <Fragment slot="title">Sign-off is a licence,<br /><span class="accent">not a verdict.</span></Fragment>
      <p>Boards treat AI approval as a one-off moment. But the model they approved can be updated by the vendor, fed new data, given new permissions, connected to new tools or used in new ways. Then it is no longer the thing they approved. Not every update needs the board, but material changes deserve a fresh look.</p>
    </SectionHead>

    <div class="gap__story" data-gap>
      <div class="gap__stage">
        <div class="licence" data-licence data-step="0" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="licence__head">
            <span class="label">AI system licence</span>
            <span class="label">No. 0042</span>
          </div>
          <div class="licence__title">
            <svg class="licence__shield" viewBox="0 0 32 32">
              <path d="M16 2.5 L27 6.5 V15.5 C27 22 22.5 26.8 16 29.5 C9.5 26.8 5 22 5 15.5 V6.5 Z" />
              <path class="licence__tick" d="M11 16 L14.5 19.5 L21 12.5" />
            </svg>
            <span>Customer assist</span>
            <span class="licence__ok">Approved</span>
          </div>
          <dl class="licence__rows">
            {rows.map((r, i) => (
              <div class="licence__row" data-row={i + 1}>
                <dt class="label">{r.dt}</dt>
                <dd>
                  <span class="licence__was">{r.was}</span>
                  <span class="licence__now">{r.now}</span>
                </dd>
                <span class="licence__flag">Changed</span>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
          <div class="licence__foot">
            <span class="label">Matches what the board approved</span>
            <span class="licence__match">
              {[0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => <span style={`--i:${i}`}></span>)}
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="licence__stamp licence__stamp--bad">Not what<br />you approved</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ol class="gap__steps">
        {drift.map((d, i) => (
          <li class="gap__step" data-step={i}>
            <p class="label gap__label">{d.label}</p>
            <p class="gap__title">{d.title}</p>
            <p class="gap__body">{d.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
        <li class="gap__step gap__step--end" data-step="5">
          <p class="gap__title">Same name. Same contract. <span class="accent">Different system.</span></p>
          <p class="gap__body">The poster asks the uncomfortable questions. Below are the kinds of answers a board could look for.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
